// The Root Chapel (Chapel_2): Teodor teaches Inkthread, the Unwriters' solvent-line reversed (bible 4.3).
// And the Lantern Grove vigil (Grove_2): eleven lanterns, eleven villages, in the present tense. No choices (8.3).

title: RootChapel_Teodor_Thread
---
<<if has_flag("verdance.teodor.thread")>>
    Teodor: The line holds. Draw it the way you would draw a road you mean to walk back along. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if not has_flag("verdance.teodor.met")>>
    Teodor: The chapel is for the brothers, cartographer. Come up to the cloister first. I will find you.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Teodor: The Cantors draw a line to let go. A thread of solvent, from the place to nothing.
Teodor: Draw it the other way. It is the same line. #plant:5.6
-> From the place to me.
    Teodor: Yes. From the place to you. Then it holds your weight, because you are holding it.
-> That's a Guild tether.
    Teodor: A tether goes into the white. This goes across it. The Guild never learned the difference.
-> ...
    Teodor: Watch the root, not your hand. There. Again.
Teodor: The birds who built this chapel crossed to the grove without a thread. We need one. It is enough.
<<grant Inkthread>>
<<flag verdance.teodor.thread 1>>
===

title: Grove_Teodor_Vigil
---
<<if has_flag("verdance.grove.vigil")>>
    Teodor: Eleven. They are all here tonight. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Teodor: Sit. There is nothing to say. I will say it anyway.
Teodor: Wenlow has a well with a crooked bucket. Nobody fixes it. They like the sound.
Teodor: Harrowby bakes on the seventh day. The whole lane smells of it.
Teodor: Coldmere is cold. It says so on the sign.
Teodor: Ashcross has two churches and one bell between them. They argue about it every Sunday.
Teodor: Nettlecombe keeps bees. The bees are not anchored. They leave every spring and come back.
Teodor: Brindle is small. Brindle is very small.
Teodor: Fenn has a ferry that crosses a river that is not there any more. The ferryman is patient.
Teodor: Scarsby has a school. The same eleven children are in it.
Teodor: Tollan is on a hill. You can see Halden from it on a clear day.
Teodor: Ettle is where my mother lives. She is seventy. She is always seventy.
Teodor: Marrowgate is the last. Marrowgate is waiting for me to be sure.
Teodor: That is all of them. Thank you for sitting.
<<flag verdance.grove.vigil 1>>
===
